romotion is the board for growing credible public reach for Post Fiat by amplifying official X posts and improving the public website at postfiatorg.github.io. The packet shows seven proposed tasks and one active task with a submitted verification response; it does not show that the website fix is merged, paid, or otherwise terminally resolved. Site work is gated on a merged pull request, and promotion tasks are supposed to rely on official sources and network payment rules.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- Accurate onboarding and official-source amplification turn attention into qualified contributors rather than noise; fixing misleading agent-setup and first-task copy directly improves the funnel into Task Node.\n- The merged-PR payment gate ties PFT rewards to verifiable work, which protects treasury credibility and makes contributor payouts defensible.\n- The current task mix also shows a risk: multiple overlapping X tasks require merged PRs, while the packet shows repeated refused X tasks at 0 PFT. Clearing that structural mismatch is the highest-leverage way to increase real promotion throughput and PFT utility.\n\n## Current Point People\n- @wizbubba: the only project-leader context in the packet; comment hivectx_22e9aee8-2e18-4f97-8260-b5845aa51d8f says \"get after it boys,\" indicating board-level direction.\n- acct_REDACTED: submitted the verification response on task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2 for the agents.md/website fix; this is the only active task awaiting review.\n- @Mrmickross: proposed task_1b91ee8f39dec4b707fb1e31a13af8f7, which combines an X post with a website onboarding PR; the packet also shows a prior refused site task, task_cbdeb4dccc98f18d66fb52c6558a37ef, so the packet does not show a completed site close from this account.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Review/QA operator: needed now to adjudicate task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2 against the merged-PR, diff, build, and Discord-proof requirements.\n- Project leader/campaign operator: needed to own task_773b44c9cd3ef2271f191938e44fb1ad and turn the seven-day sprint into a live operating cadence with a single evidence template.\n- Website maintainer/reviewer: needed to merge or reject the overlapping onboarding/agent-setup PRs from task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2, task_1b91ee8f39dec4b707fb1e31a13af8f7, and task_c461bdd9bfb4d67352f04a618dedd129 without conflicting edits.\n- KOL/amplification operators with linked GitHub accounts: needed for the proposed X tasks, but only after the PR evidence path is made operationally clear.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Clear the review queue first: review task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2 now. Verify the PR is authored by the linked GitHub account, merged into main after task creation, changes content/agents.md as described, includes passing build evidence, and has the required Discord announcement. If any proof is missing, reject with the exact missing item rather than leaving it pending.\n- Fix the PR-gate mismatch before generating more promotion tasks. The proposed X tasks task_1b91ee8f39dec4b707fb1e31a13af8f7, task_c461bdd9bfb4d67352f04a618dedd129, task_4616ccd5ce520e616cb9514069c13ebe, task_f7b9ddf3b36e3e338c90c49ce86d25e8, task_66effcc29c399364463c9b287c69c506, and task_ce765634963a5d34e7afd7da752afac9 all require merged PRs, but the packet shows repeated refused X tasks at 0 PFT. Define one canonical, low-friction PR target for amplification records, or split X-only proof from PR payment, so contributors are not asked to satisfy an unclear duplicate gate.\n- Sequence accuracy before amplification: merge the website/onboarding fixes first, then have KOL tasks amplify the corrected pages. For task_773b44c9cd3ef2271f191938e44fb1ad, require a live source check before each post because the packet says the latest official X post is dated September 25 and is outside the 14-day freshness window; also resolve the conflict with task_ce765634963a5d34e7afd7da752afac9, which explicitly allows an older announcement.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Make accuracy the campaign: clear the website/agent-setup review, merge the onboarding fixes, then amplify the corrected official pages with a small number of well-briefed KOLs. Replace overlapping one-off X tasks with a single sprint/evidence template and a canonical PR target so the payment gate is satisfiable. Measure success by merged fixes, accurate live posts, and qualified newcomer traffic, not by task volume.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Pause new overlapping amplification task generation. First adjudicate task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2, then consolidate the proposed X tasks around one canonical PR evidence path and one live-source freshness rule; assign task_773b44c9cd3ef2271f191938e44fb1ad to a project_leader and only route KOL tasks after the PR gate is operationally clear.","sourcePacketDigest":"27334dd6e63dfe69dc8803a57abd84c90c111ef23d08b2c00fc2d4c2a7a7aec9","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":8,"boardCommentCount":1,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":29,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":1},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0145176,"latencyMs":44834,"inputTokens":25304,"totalTokens":31076,"outputTokens":5772,"reasoningTokens":4514},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-12T20:34:44.912Z","createdAt":"2026-11-12T20:34:44.951Z"},"tasksInFlight":8,"terminalTaskCount":69,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_d82280db72dad1717323f53e1d9937e2","title":"Clarify Agent Setup Instructions and Merge Website Fix","state":"verification_response_submitted","viewerScoped":false,"viewerRelation":"","viewerActive":false,"assignee":"rREDACTED","assigneeAccountId":"acct_REDACTED","assigneeHasPublicProfile":true,"assigneeHandle":"whiteguy","assigneeDisp