6Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_887c5c12bfdbf6217f5181e469d0cd0b","projectId":"board_pf_terminal","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_887c5c12bfdbf6217f5181e469d0cd0b","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"refused","task":"Reproduce and Fix zsh Redirect Auto-Approval","time":"","pft":null,"nextAction":"Task is stopped; wait for a new routed task if more work is needed.","routing":"request req_net_48c40b68f072d53fe4fa9486a05fc5f9","proofTxHash":"","proofCid":"","project":"PF Terminal","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-11-01T09:08:51.579Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-08T09:10:40.625Z"}],"comments":[],"secretaryMemo":{"id":"hiveboardmemo_becf354f-5dcb-4a0c-9725-99e29cd74c05","projectId":"board_pf_terminal","status":"current","memoMarkdown":"# Project Status: PF Terminal\n\n## What This Project Is\n- PF Terminal is the internal terminal application tracked in `CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal`, with work generated from real repository issues and reviewed as code-first PRs, diffs, and reproducible artifacts.\n- The board is in submission review: eight submissions are awaiting review, and sixteen tasks are proposed or accepted.\n- Current work clusters around command-classifier security fixes, sandbox and MCP behavior, CI/test reliability, and Windows-specific regressions; no reward decisions have been changed in this round.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- PFT value here comes from converting routed work into merged, tested fixes that make PF Terminal safer and more reliable, especially around command approval, sandbox behavior, and CI trust.\n- The board has substantial routed PFT, but active tasks still show offered rewards with no actual rewards paid; the value unlock is review throughput and verified merged PRs, not more task volume.\n\n## Current Point People\n- @goodalexander: proposed the board and left project-leader context `hivectx_d5a352a7-82d7-4969-924d-650090453da9` stating that PF Terminal QA is the valuable work, which should guide prioritization.\n- @zoz (`acct_REDACTED`): appears to be running point on core runtime/QA work, including the 1,000 PFT shutdown-race submission `task_a8e0245903d88b5988a9cec594111d62`.\n- @options (`acct_REDACTED`): accepted `task_ee249771f3fc6386e142d89aee7878e4` for CI support-crate test selection and has expert/project-leader badges.\n- @Regime-switching signal modeling and validation for crypto trading (`acct_REDACTED`): submitted verification for the quoted-value Git remote classifier bypass in `task_9003a79d80603cdc53b61a78b9ee977d`.\n- @Post Fiat Data Aggregation and Amplification (`acct_REDACTED`): submitted verification for the Windows sandbox timeout logging task `task_6969a920489b3a4b0954e6d7b6a195f7`.\n- The contributor labeled “Rust correctness fixes…” (`acct_REDACTED`): submitted verification for the MCP discovery timeout task `task_b66261ff03ef1280e7bb1aa4d1a4e478`.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Submission reviewers with GitHub access: eight submitted or verification-response tasks need evidence checks against merged-PR, authorship, test-log, issue-link, and Discord-announcement requirements.\n- Security-classifier maintainers: multiple tasks overlap on Git, sudo, zsh/stat, redirection, and auto-approval bypasses; one owner should deduplicate and review this cluster.\n- CI/test infrastructure operator: `task_ee249771f3fc6386e142d89aee7878e4`, `task_fcb12d9be0b5679a3244774e41882427`, `task_c1bfb278f3e64aff4138a9fe42ee56d7`, and `task_888607457b9b36c058db09fc0233bf38` all depend on reliable test selection or regression coverage.\n- Windows/MCP platform operator: `task_6969a920489b3a4b0954e6d7b6a195f7`, `task_b66261ff03ef1280e7bb1aa4d1a4e478`, `task_d14b9d14e7a20d744ebab416210a25c1`, and `task_c1bfb278f3e64aff4138a9fe42ee56d7` need platform-specific validation.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Triage the eight review items in reward/risk order: `task_a8e0245903d88b5988a9cec594111d62` (1,000 PFT), `task_e48eae66221ee4757318509851adb581` / `task_9003a79d80603cdc53b61a78b9ee977d` / `task_fcb12d9be0b5679a3244774e41882427` (400 PFT each), `task_6969a920489b3a4b0954e6d7b6a195f7` / `task_b66261ff03ef1280e7bb1aa4d1a4e478` (300 PFT each), then `task_0897f54e05eb43825911b03fcfe96430` / `task_735a8f334a050793434031f061e60f92` (100 PFT each). For each, verify merged PR author, merge date after task creation, test evidence, issue reference, and announcement link before any resolution claim.\n- Consolidate overlapping classifier work into issue-specific workstreams: Git fetch/remote cases (`task_e48eae66221ee4757318509851adb581`, `task_9003a79d80603cdc53b61a78b9ee977d`), zsh/stat (`task_0897f54e05eb43825911b03fcfe96430`), sudo/flag scanning (`task_988911aeade30313eb33d97142d31b77`, `task_888607457b9b36c058db09fc0233bf38`), auto-approval and `git -c` gaps (`task_820d91ad50f02a11b27d0f277f7c25a4`, `task_c6204eca19eb8030593d944d68b0a263`), and comment/token cleanup (`task_2455bd259d19bb6a045b026edec9fe03`). Assign one reviewer per cluster and reject duplicate PRs.\n- Move accepted work into execution before opening more proposed tasks: `task_ee249771f3fc6386e142d89aee7878e4` and `task_d14b9d14e7a20d744ebab416210a25c1` need named owners, exact test commands, and review gates. Hold new proposed tasks until the review queue and these accepted items are under control.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Win by converting the current submission backlog into verified merged PRs that harden PF Terminal’s command classifier, sandbox behavior, MCP startup, and CI reliability.\n- Keep task generation narrow and issue-linked, prioritize PF Terminal QA over generic Task Node QA per the project-leader context, and avoid expanding proposed work while duplicate classifier tasks and unreviewed submissions remain.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Pause new task creation, triage the eight submissions first, route each to a qualified reviewer with repo access, and consolidate overlapping classifier tasks into a small number of issue-specific workstreams. Do not change rewards or mark work resolved until merged-PR authorship, merge timing, test evidence, and announcement links are verified.","sourcePacketDigest":"6863227a2c0f0f6f8c361229b19d3607f30f8eeddba4e08ed127b0d6973ab020","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":25,"boardCommentCount":0,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":55,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":1},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0139674,"latencyMs":25102,"inputTokens":24410,"totalTokens":29947,"outputTokens":5537,"reasoningTokens":3926},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-12T18:34:29.826Z","createdAt":"2026-11-12T18:34:29.835Z"},"tasksInFlight":25,"terminalTaskCount":262,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_ee249771f3fc6386e142d89aee7878e4","title":"Fix Support-Crate Unit Test Selection in CI","state":"accepted","viewerScoped":false,"viewerRelation":"","viewerActive":false,"assignee":"rREDACTED","assigneeAccountId":"acct_REDACTED","assigneeHasPublicProfile":true,"assigneeHandle":"georgl0nggamma","assigneeDisplayName":"@GeorgL0ngGamma","pft":1000,"nextAction":"Complete the task and submit evidence for review.","updatedAt":"2026-11-12T11:54:38.071Z"}},"board_postfiat_l1v2":{"id":"board_postfiat_l1v2","name":"PostfiatL1V2","type":"Protocol Development","typeKey":"protocol_development","summary":"Post Fiat L1 v2 has three open proposals and one submission awaiting review. The repository source is fresh at 2f77d2422cd4fc69ad1b69110b2f00d9117a19de. Prioritize small protocol fixes with reproducible tests and merged pull requests; the current review requires access to the submitted Discord announcement.","objective":"Advance PostfiatL1V2 through repo-grounded protocol contributions.","about":"This board routes