"updatedAt":"2026-09-25T20:51:22.899Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_10ac2fed3ce020d2e04f3d55344a5ea8","projectId":"board_postfiat_l1v2","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_10ac2fed3ce020d2e04f3d55344a5ea8","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"whiteguy","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"rewarded","task":"Verify Issue #26 Unsafe-Flag Bug Status on Main","time":"","pft":100,"nextAction":"Reward paid. View proof, copy the tx, or request another task.","routing":"request req_net_e7217f05673eb044233b875700b23565","proofTxHash":"9AFC1CE1B7CC8840468D93EB80F273754EE15CFFE7A85F5D0C873921757D96A5","proofCid":"Qmb64upj4Uui9yWahWVk2XhPz9yiM886Edz8f1RjbKi1rN","project":"PostfiatL1V2","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-09-25T17:49:12.731Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-25T19:09:58.227Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_d87f70539fb301f4e05325ab7bdf3b50","projectId":"board_postfiat_l1v2","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_d87f70539fb301f4e05325ab7bdf3b50","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"whiteguy","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"rewarded","task":"Audit Issue 36 Operator Onboarding Gaps and Publish Coverage Gist","time":"","pft":100,"nextAction":"Reward paid. View proof, copy the tx, or request another task.","routing":"request req_net_ed16fa550ab50c72d36ead4ab655bbf0","proofTxHash":"8BAA97F00DEB3FD290C8D3E5F279D74E6E8CE2F1E2DED3800D80F27840441100","proofCid":"QmPhCJ2u5PGdsc5LwBm6hSYXRND9odynwycMAgLqndbdYj","project":"PostfiatL1V2","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-09-25T13:01:30.112Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-25T17:46:37.993Z"}],"comments":[],"secretaryMemo":{"id":"hiveboardmemo_711a34de-5093-4516-a2e0-2e558a950d9e","projectId":"board_postfiat_l1v2","status":"current","memoMarkdown":"# Project Status: PostfiatL1V2\n\n## What This Project Is\n- PostfiatL1V2 is a protocol-development board for the second version of Post Fiat L1, routing repo-grounded work in `postfiatorg/postfiatl1v2`.\n- Current work centers on Orchard privacy/secret-handling fixes, testnet monitor redaction, a two-sprint hardening plan, and one README-grounded public announcement.\n- The board has five active tasks: one verification response submitted and four proposed.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- PFT value depends on a credible, secure L1 and a reliable testnet; merged, tested protocol fixes reduce security and operational risk.\n- The highest-value work is conversion of proposals into merged PRs with reproducible tests, not additional task volume.\n- Accurate public communication can amplify verified milestones, but only after code and README evidence exists.\n\n## Current Point People\n- Post Fiat infrastructure account (`acct_REDACTED`): has the only active task past proposal, `task_e597f4abd43cd65380f7e6129fc388ad`, in `verification_response_submitted` for Orchard secret zeroization; also has prior monitor/bridge security tasks, so appears closest to security-hardening review.\n- `@goodalexander`: proposed the board and has active `task_dae63c4ebbd1f86bce26373b6a2af90a` for reducing Orchard spending-key copies; likely protocol/security direction.\n- `@LLM pipelines`: has active `task_81bc71d40d0380d4508a5a7e82021ac0` for IPv6 redaction in testnet monitor logs; prior rewarded work on a node data-dir RPC fix supports a testnet/monitor operator read.\n- `@surfcoderepeat`: has active `task_dfdf10f43ee08a6d2acfb9da1265a521` for the Lock/bridge Phase 2 X post; comms point for README-grounded messaging.\n- No board comments or project-leader context are present in the packet; point-person reads are inferred from active task associations.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Rust/Orchard security reviewer: needed now to adjudicate `task_e597f4abd43cd65380f7e6129fc388ad` and later review `task_dae63c4ebbd1f86bce26373b6a2af90a` for API and secret-lifetime correctness.\n- Python/testnet monitor operator: needed to execute `task_81bc71d40d0380d4508a5a7e82021ac0` with IPv6 regression tests and a merged PR.\n- Project leader/protocol planner: needed to turn `task_52041e812c77bd140a528f471ceb4dea` into a merged two-sprint plan with named owners and review gates.\n- KOL/communications operator: needed for `task_dfdf10f43ee08a6d2acfb9da1265a521`, but only after README claims are checked and the post is tied to repository evidence.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Resolve `task_e597f4abd43cd65380f7e6129fc388ad` first: review the submitted verification response against issue #181 points 3 and 5, requiring a merged PR URL, test commands/results, type-by-type zeroization documentation, and Discord announcement proof. If evidence is incomplete, return it with exact gaps.\n- Route `task_81bc71d40d0380d4508a5a7e82021ac0` to an available expert Python/testnet operator now; it is a bounded 1,000 PFT fix with clear regression requirements for bracketed IPv6, compressed IPv6, IPv4 controls, and loopback preservation.\n- Sequence Orchard work: hold `task_dae63c4ebbd1f86bce26373b6a2af90a` until the `verify.rs` review overlap with `task_e597f4abd43cd65380f7e6129fc388ad` is clear, then require borrowed/zeroizing inputs, safe caller updates, API compatibility notes, and `cargo test -p postfiat-privacy-orchard --locked`.\n- Use `task_52041e812c77bd140a528f471ceb4dea` to publish a merged two-sprint plan with issue/PR/CI evidence, named owners, dependencies, and review gates, but do not let planning displace code merges.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Prioritize merged, tested security and reliability fixes over new task generation.\n- Clear the Orchard review queue, land the IPv6 redaction, and use the two-sprint plan to coordinate owners and review gates.\n- Keep public comms tied to verified README/code evidence; do not amplify or pay out until merged PRs and tests exist.\n- Avoid re-issuing near-duplicate monitor/bridge/Python tasks without checking current state, since the terminal history contains multiple refused or cancelled tasks in adjacent scopes.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Do not create new tasks yet. Keep `task_e597f4abd43cd65380f7e6129fc388ad` in review with a strict evidence checklist, route `task_81bc71d40d0380d4508a5a7e82021ac0` to an available expert Python/testnet operator, gate `task_dae63c4ebbd1f86bce26373b6a2af90a` on the `verify.rs` review, and require `task_52041e812c77bd140a528f471ceb4dea` to name owners and gates. Hold `task_dfdf10f43ee08a6d2acfb9da1265a521` until README claims are checked.","sourcePacketDigest":"c8474e221e2cf6594246ec302691afb391d121a55f7c684344298bdbe8f75f0a","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":5,"boardCommentCount":0,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":26,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":0},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0133947,"latencyMs":38717,"inputTokens":26337,"totalTokens":30915,"outputTokens":4578,"reasoningTokens":3304},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-12T18:35:10.160Z","createdAt":"2026-11-12T18:35:10.232Z"},"tasksInFlight":6,"terminalTaskCount":66,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_7be5fe24a25117f2d02b1e5232d00bad","title":"Test and Fix Testnet Proof-Latency Warnings","state":"accepted","viewerScoped":false,"viewerRelation":"","viewerActive":false,"assignee":"rREDACTED","assigneeAccountId":"acct_REDACTED","assigneeHasPublicProfile":true,"assigneeHandle":"walkonwayvs","assigneeDisplayName":"walkonwayvs","pft":1000,"nextAction":"Complete the task and submit evidence for review.","updatedAt":"2026-11-12T23:34:34.236Z"}},"board_ai_l1_governance":{"id":"board_ai_l1_governance","name":"AI Layer 1 Governance","type":"Network Validation","typeKey":"network_validation","summary":"AI L1 Governance: four tasks are open, including one accepted scoring task. Prioritize tested governance replay and validator-scoring work; the accepted task remains pendi