:"AI Layer 1 Governance","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-08-15T01:51:21.060Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-15T03:46:36.009Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_5e57d078b181d9da70cb64326af72626","projectId":"board_ai_l1_governance","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_5e57d078b181d9da70cb64326af72626","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"wizbubba","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"refused","task":"Write Implementation Plan for G.5.6 Governance Decision Step","time":"","pft":null,"nextAction":"Task is stopped; wait for a new routed task if more work is needed.","routing":"request req_net_a11955fd8c9c211c2f817efef2b3d841","proofTxHash":"","proofCid":"","project":"AI Layer 1 Governance","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-08-15T01:53:36.573Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-15T03:08:48.961Z"}],"comments":[],"secretaryMemo":{"id":"hiveboardmemo_89e0b0cb-dcba-443f-b9a7-46cb8b81e4a4","projectId":"board_ai_l1_governance","status":"current","memoMarkdown":"# Project Status: AI Layer 1 Governance\n\n## What This Project Is\n- AI Layer 1 Governance is a network-validation board for the XRPL fork’s governance replay and the supporting dynamic UNL scoring service.\n- It routes work against `postfiatd`, `rippled`, and `dynamic-unl-scoring`, with 30,850 PFT routed and 64 planned tasks.\n- The packet shows three proposed active tasks; the summary’s mention of a fourth “accepted scoring task” is not reflected in the active task list and should be reconciled.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- PFT value depends on a credible L1: deterministic governance replay and correct validator scoring reduce the risk of governance errors, validator mis-selection, and unverifiable network behavior.\n- The active tasks target merged code and regression tests, which is the kind of checkable work that can justify token routing.\n- Evidence discipline matters here because the terminal history is dominated by refused or cancelled tasks; unmerged work should not be treated as resolved value.\n\n## Current Point People\n- `@Post-quantum cryptography, blockchain integrity audit, and verified engineering analysis` (`acct_REDACTED`): assigned `task_587f6ae356e2a0e5ffdf037e99d69d70` for the amendment-vote replay regression test.\n- `acct_REDACTED`: assigned `task_8ff1d15d0b9af6e637ab41b5d0d9f8f5` for the merged AI governance replay sprint plan; the task requires a `project_leader` operating badge.\n- `@0xPostFiatChad` (`acct_REDACTED`): assigned `task_b84d1f5b83578c362961c0abf572308e`, the 5,000 PFT core-repo edge-case fix.\n- No `projectLeaderContext` is supplied, so point-person status is inferred from active task assignment rather than confirmed leadership routing.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Expert XRPL/C++ governance-replay tester: `task_587f6ae356e2a0e5ffdf037e99d69d70` needs an `expert_bundle` merged PR with deterministic replay evidence, and no progress is shown.\n- Core contributor / UNL scoring engineer: `task_b84d1f5b83578c362961c0abf572308e` is the highest-reward active task and needs a reproducible edge-case fix plus regression test.\n- Project leader / review coordinator: `task_8ff1d15d0b9af6e637ab41b5d0d9f8f5` needs to name owners, dependencies, and review gates, and can help reconcile the active-task discrepancy.\n- QA/evidence preflight reviewer: many terminal tasks are refused or cancelled, while active tasks require merged PRs; preflight can stop invalid submissions before they consume review time.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Make `task_b84d1f5b83578c362961c0abf572308e` the first execution priority: require `@0xPostFiatChad` to pin one UNL-scoring or governance-replay edge case, show failing-before/passing-after tests, and merge the PR into main.\n- Run `task_587f6ae356e2a0e5ffdf037e99d69d70` as the governance-replay proof lane: two validation orders, each run twice, identical vote actions and majority/enabled states at threshold and after hold time, deterministic state-trace hashes, and no production consensus changes.\n- Use `task_8ff1d15d0b9af6e637ab41b5d0d9f8f5` as a coordination gate: require named owners for the two code tasks, explicit review gates, dependencies, and a first post-merge action; reconcile the summary’s “four open tasks / accepted scoring task” claim against the three proposed active tasks before routing more work.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Concentrate board energy on merged, tested code in `postfiatd` and `dynamic-unl-scoring`.\n- Use the sprint plan only to sequence work and assign review, not as a substitute for code delivery.\n- Enforce merged-PR evidence and do not treat refused or cancelled terminal tasks as proof that prior defects are fixed; PFT value comes from verifiable governance and scoring reliability.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Prioritize `task_b84d1f5b83578c362961c0abf572308e` and `task_587f6ae356e2a0e5ffdf037e99d69d70`, keep `task_8ff1d15d0b9af6e637ab41b5d0d9f8f5` as a coordination gate, and preflight each assignee’s badge/capacity and merged-PR evidence before more routing.\n- Reconcile the active-task count conflict and do not mark any governance fix resolved without a merged PR and test evidence.","sourcePacketDigest":"c953faf0dd6c2a1cfff6e77a539cd407c0a274787bf484d1797431ce8921a998","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":3,"boardCommentCount":0,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":21,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":0},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0145056,"latencyMs":36438,"inputTokens":25824,"totalTokens":31456,"outputTokens":5632,"reasoningTokens":4514},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-13T00:34:36.924Z","createdAt":"2026-11-13T00:34:36.926Z"},"tasksInFlight":3,"terminalTaskCount":61,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_b84d1f5b83578c362961c0abf572308e","title":"Fix and Test O