true,"hiveHandle":"goodalexander","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"rewarded","task":"Prevent Diverged Checkouts From Supplying Project Commits","time":"","pft":250,"nextAction":"Reward paid. View proof, copy the tx, or request another task.","routing":"request req_net_c7f9568acf163225cb9ef898f5119aed","proofTxHash":"37658776F6745C33E998CB701B05DA16B1591118E6FA0765176F01BD9B5CA2C1","proofCid":"QmYxdkGUg7Bk5GWD4KX6s2YjJ1MeQDzeZoB2CAXATkoc9z","project":"Task Node Fixes","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-08-06T21:20:35.841Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T19:37:36.080Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_3a218afd9aa8f0ac2fdb6864fb5e06a3","projectId":"board_tasknode_fixes","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_3a218afd9aa8f0ac2fdb6864fb5e06a3","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"goodalexander","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"rewarded","task":"Harden Board Task Creation Against Database Timeouts","time":"","pft":500,"nextAction":"Reward paid. View proof, copy the tx, or request another task.","routing":"request req_net_84a4fd1975344b8dd9d22c6eea9e84df","proofTxHash":"1806D13B8D0CC14A7B6F6E33EAD3A922E696B22549F3AC4D4549159ECEF19B6E","proofCid":"QmQFzjeov88yx5emRRV9682SLd3GRGmzTTWWEzcTceizsj","project":"Task Node Fixes","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-08-06T21:05:30.968Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T19:34:03.362Z"}],"comments":[],"secretaryMemo":{"id":"hiveboardmemo_30541219-c75e-4dc7-bcaf-969039819cc0","projectId":"board_tasknode_fixes","status":"current","memoMarkdown":"# Project Status: Task Node Fixes\n\n## What This Project Is\n- Task Node Fixes is a protocol-applications board for repairing and hardening Task Node, the system that serves board packets, Hive context, and task workflow status.\n- The board is in defect triage with three proposed code tasks, all assigned to @goodalexander because the packet says only he has code access to the Task Node deployment.\n- No submissions are awaiting review; the terminal tasks shown are refused with zero actual reward, so they are not evidence that the underlying defects were fixed.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- Task Node is the operating surface for routing PFT-funded work and showing operators whether project context is fresh, complete, and responsive.\n- Fixing stale Hive Secretary status, Hive Context row omission, and slow board packets improves trust in board decisions, reduces wasted operator cycles, and protects a board with 28,971 PFT routed through it.\n- Reliable status and packet behavior make it easier to route real work, verify submissions, and pay contributors without misleading evidence.\n\n## Current Point People\n- @goodalexander: proposer of the board, sole code-access holder, and assignee on all three active tasks: task_e7866dab1584e41cf84ed02017f11c41, task_3bd34eb6dce4ba7295fade67d86eb4f3, and task_70bcb8756822b8ea2837566190851974.\n- No other point person is evidenced: projectLeaderContext is empty, and the board’s own rule restricts fixes to @goodalexander despite 52 eligible contributors appearing in the packet.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Code owner/implementer: @goodalexander to reproduce, patch, test, and land the three proposed fixes; no other assignee is eligible under the board’s code-access constraint.\n- Independent QA/review operator: a QA worker or core contributor to verify before/after API behavior and test output, without taking code ownership.\n- Merge/release reviewer: someone with repository merge authority to ensure each fix lands as a merged PR, since the submission requirements reject open, draft, or closed-unmerged PRs.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Lead with task_e7866dab1584e41cf84ed02017f11c41, the 1,000 PFT stale Hive Secretary task: reproduce by comparing `/api/hive/context` report age and source digest against `/api/system/status` worker status, add an age threshold and targeted tests, and require before/after evidence showing the old report is not labeled Current.\n- Then take task_70bcb8756822b8ea2837566190851974: fix Hive Context selection so newest non-deleted rows are ordered before `LIMIT`, with regression tests for `limit=120` vs `limit=240`, deleted-row exclusion, and stable timestamp/ID ordering.\n- Treat task_3bd34eb6dce4ba7295fade67d86eb4f3 as an intermittent performance investigation: reproduce concurrent board requests against a task-detail control, capture timings, identify the bottleneck, and preserve visible stale/unavailable source status rather than hiding it.\n- Before creating any new task, deduplicate against issues #376 and #377 and the refused terminal tasks; route only to @goodalexander and require merged PR, targeted test output, before/after API evidence, and Discord announcement evidence.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Run this board as a narrow repair queue, not a broad contributor marketplace. Concentrate scarce code access on the three trust-and-throughput defects, force reproducible evidence and merged PRs, and use independent QA to prevent stale or misleading status from being marked fixed.\n- Keep the single-assignee constraint until code access is expanded; adding more contributors without access would create routing noise rather than shipped fixes.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Do not create new tasks yet. Keep the three proposed tasks with @goodalexander, sequence them stale-status → Hive-context ordering → slow packets, and require reproduction, targeted tests, merged PR, before/after API evidence, and Discord announcement before review. Check duplicates against issues #376/#377 and refused terminal tasks, and do not treat refused tasks as resolved.","sourcePacketDigest":"3b5c3e3613532d3c36de8910c8e3c867a1ed64b542d17e6f500b9d172b04d1a8","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":3,"boardCommentCount":0,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":6,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":0},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0143619,"latencyMs":29721,"inputTokens":26201,"totalTokens":31619,"outputTokens":5418,"reasoningTokens":4514},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-12T15:20:04.285Z","createdAt":"2026-11-12T15:20:04.310Z"},"tasksInFlight":3,"terminalTaskCount":46,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_e7866dab1584e41cf84ed02017f11c41","title":"Fix Stale Hive Secretary Status and Add Tests","state":"proposed","viewerScoped":false,"viewerRelation":"","viewerActive":false,"assignee":"rREDACTED","assigneeAccountId":"acct_REDACTED","assigneeHasPublicProfile":true,"assigneeHandle":"goodalexander","assigneeDisplayName":"@goodalexander","pft":1000,"nextAction":"Open the task and accept or refuse it before the deadline.","updatedAt":"2026-11-10T23:26:24.342Z"}},"board_capital_markets":{"id":"board_capital_markets","name":"Capital Markets","type":"Alpha Generation","typeKey":"alpha_generation","summary":"Capital Markets has one proposed research sprint task and no submissions awaiting review. The public research repository and AGTI website were refreshed on November 12; the mapped AGTI repository returned HTTP 404. Candidate eligibility conflicts require operator reconciliation before affected accounts can be routed. Research tasks require reproducible code and a merged pull request.","objective":"Engage with AGTI and community capital-markets research; route credible alpha ideas into reviewable artifacts.","about":"This board routes capital markets engagement: AGTI research, goodalexander's public work, and community-sourced alpha ideas. Context repos are goodalexander.github.io and agti, plus agti.net.","status":"active","priority":60,"origin":"operator_seed","proposedBy":"goodalexander","proposed":"Aug 5, 2026","phase":"Research intake","phaseCurrent":0,"phaseTotal":0,"pft":24715,"taskCount":93,"contributorCount":25,"plannedPftTarget":25300,"plannedTaskCoun