ts","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-09-23T02:46:47.223Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T12:52:30.106Z"},{"id":"project_task_activity_task_d6d8ba57d14fd0252d1a291330158674","projectId":"board_capital_markets","wallet":"rREDACTED","taskId":"task_d6d8ba57d14fd0252d1a291330158674","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfile":true,"hiveHandle":"georgl0nggamma","displayName":"REDACTED","action":"rewarded","task":"Publish Claim-By-Claim Audit Of AI Productivity Paradox Essay","time":"","pft":100,"nextAction":"Reward paid. View proof, copy the tx, or request another task.","routing":"request req_net_085401576f0428f426d5a7572e6239c5","proofTxHash":"DF4518285324CCC9DBD527AFD912CEEC5F71DA312DE3F15F217534A5DDC99D83","proofCid":"QmQ7nw9Mu2Uf6BJMehkMgwPVFQTnZE3rpH88LWrGybxr3q","project":"Capital Markets","derived":true,"createdAt":"2026-09-22T15:40:01.303Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-23T11:16:41.305Z"}],"comments":[],"secretaryMemo":{"id":"hiveboardmemo_ea1888e6-e047-41c7-a0e5-514007fd2a5b","projectId":"board_capital_markets","status":"current","memoMarkdown":"# Project Status: Capital Markets\n\n## What This Project Is\n- Capital Markets is a research-intake board for AGTI, goodalexander’s public market work, and community-sourced alpha ideas, with the goal of routing credible ideas into reviewable artifacts. It currently has one proposed task, “Merge a One-Week Capital Markets Research Sprint Plan” (`task_369857937afc3221bd8c12327a8e319b`, 5,000 PFT offered), and no submissions awaiting review. The packet also flags two operating blockers: candidate eligibility conflicts need operator reconciliation, and the mapped AGTI repository returned HTTP 404 even though the public research repository and AGTI website were refreshed on November 12.\n\n## Why This Advances PFT Value\n- PFT value depends on the network converting attention and community ideas into verifiable work, not just posts. A merged sprint plan with three named ideas, owners, schedules, and evidence standards would create a concrete pipeline from capital-markets research to reproducible code and merged PRs, making PFT rewards more credibly tied to real research and coordination. Fixing eligibility and evidence conflicts also reduces wasted rewards on refused or unpayable tasks.\n\n## Current Point People\n- goodalexander: board proposer and the only project-leader context in the packet; the board’s sources are AGTI, goodalexander’s public work, and community alpha.\n- acct_REDACTED: sole active-task contributor for the sprint-plan task (`task_369857937afc3221bd8c12327a8e319b`), which requires the `project_leader` badge; the packet does not show a handle for this account.\n- No separate current reviewer or board manager is evidenced; historical rewarded contributors such as @options, @zoz, and @CFO working-capital and operating metrics trackers appear in terminal history but are not shown as current owners.\n\n## Operators Needed\n- Project leader with GitHub merge rights: needed to land the sprint plan as a merged PR and prevent another open/draft-only submission.\n- Eligibility/repo reconciliation operator: needed now to resolve candidate eligibility conflicts and the AGTI repository 404 before affected accounts are routed.\n- Research QA/review operator: needed to enforce the board’s stated standard of reproducible code plus a merged pull request, and to reject public-post-only evidence where the task requires a merged PR.\n\n## Next Tactics\n- Close the sole active task: require `acct_REDACTED` to submit a merged PR in the Capital Markets public research repository containing exactly three community-sourced ideas with source links, named owners, a one-week schedule, and evidence standards, plus an approved Post Fiat channel announcement; do not pay for open, draft, or closed PRs.\n- Run a routing-cleanup pass before generating more work: reconcile candidate eligibility conflicts, fix or replace the AGTI repository mapping that returned HTTP 404, and confirm the refreshed public research repository and AGTI website are the canonical sources.\n- Reset the task template around evidence: multiple terminal tasks are refused at 0 PFT, and some task text mixes public-post/Medium evidence with a merged-PR payment requirement. Align the required evidence with the payment rule, then prioritize reproducible-code and merged-PR research over additional low-signal KOL posts.\n\n## Overall Strategy\n- Use the one-week sprint plan as the board’s operating reset: get one merged, owner-assigned research sprint with explicit evidence standards, fix the routing and repo blockers, and then judge outputs by reproducibility and merged artifacts. Do not scale new capital-markets tasks until eligibility and evidence rules are consistent, because more volume will otherwise produce more refused work rather than PFT-value-accreting research.\n\n## Recommendation For Task Management Agent\n- Hold new task generation until the sprint-plan task is either merged or explicitly re-scoped, and route an operator to reconcile eligibility conflicts and the AGTI repo 404. After the plan merges, generate only three owner-specific research tasks with reproducible-code/merged-PR evidence and assign a named reviewer; do not create more public-post tasks under the current conflicting evidence standard.","sourcePacketDigest":"723cee66d511eb2fe52002f3ba2eba5362c83e381d380a4e3076f44c62051513","sourceCounts":{"activeTaskCount":1,"boardCommentCount":0,"terminalTaskCount":40,"omittedActiveTaskCount":0,"eligibleContributorCount":52,"omittedTerminalTaskCount":52,"pendingGenerationJobCount":0,"projectLeaderContextCount":1},"provider":"vercel","model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017","promptVersion":"glm_board_secretary_status_memo_v1","promptDigest":"2a91391300f9d46e816eaddca5d1438785746de769c08d0e44b5d3ccab7911cf","usage":{"costUsd":0.0135552,"latencyMs":18845,"inputTokens":26280,"totalTokens":31006,"outputTokens":4726,"reasoningTokens":3840},"error":"","generatedAt":"2026-11-12T22:34:39.403Z","createdAt":"2026-11-12T22:34:39.431Z"},"tasksInFlight":1,"terminalTaskCount":92,"nextTask":{"taskId":"task_369857937afc3221bd8c12327a8e319b","title":"Merge a One-Week Capital Markets Research Sprint Plan","state":"proposed","viewerScoped":false,"viewerRelation":"","viewerActive":false,"assignee":"rREDACTED","assigneeAccountId":"acct_REDACTED","assigneeHasPublicProfile":true,"assigneeHandle":"donravle","assigneeDisplayName":"@donravle","pft":5000,"nextAction":"Open the task and accept or refuse it before the deadline.","updatedAt":"2026-11-06T18:21:10.025Z"}},"board_value_accountability":{"id":"board_value_accountability","name":"Value Accountability","type":"Network Validation","typeKey":"network_validation","summary":"Value Accountability checks each flagged account for a Discord handle, one checkable Post Fiat contribution, and a brief explanation. One verification response remains outstanding and a separate existing review decision is pending publication.","objective":"Recover network value: accounts paid for banned task shapes must show market-cap accretion or be blacklisted.","about":"Accounts that earned PFT for critiques of published writing or audit/review write-ups receive one mandatory task. They must show concrete, verifiable evidence that their paid work increased Post Fiat market cap, plus a Discord sign-off from a different member. The board manager judges strictly; rejection, refusal or a missed deadline blacklists the account.","status":"active","priority":90,"origin":"operator_seed","proposedBy":"goodalexander","proposed":"Sep 26, 2026","phase":"Evidence review","phaseCurrent":0,"phaseTotal":0,"pft":163.2,"taskCount":62,"contributorCount":31,"plannedPftTarget":185.2,"plannedTaskCount":62,"plannedContributorTarget":0,"pendingGenerationCount":0,"sourceHiveSecretaryReportId":"","sourREDACTED":"","sourceInputs":{"inputs":["operator_mandate_20260926_value_accountability"]},"contributors":[{"wallet":"rREDACTED","accountId":"acct_REDACTED","hasPublicProfi